** `python -m pytest -q` â†’ **GREEN 1163 passed, 1 skipped** (global `_esc` hardening regressed nothing).\n- **VERDICT: GO â€” committed to branch (6c1c2ab).** âœ… **John signed off (\"carry on\", standing approval).** Wave 7 done.\n\n## Wave 8 â€” CLI mirror + healthcheck v10 + distro scan + docs (PROJECT DONE) â€” âœ… GREEN\n\n- **EXECUTE.** `anchor.py` read-only mirrors: `rnd boneyard <pid> [--search <q>]` (`boneyard.list_entries`/`search`, honest-empty) + `rnd next-prompt <pid> --session <id>` (record `pending_paste` â†’ durable `NEXT-PROMPT.md` â†’ rebuild via `handoff.build_next_stage_prompt`; never starts a session/model). `anchor_healthcheck.check_rnd_v10_surface` (7-step, fully stubbed; stub PTY + stream-json stub runner + temp worktree base + temp git project) registered in `main()`. CLAUDE.md v10 section + endpoint table + file structure + CLI bullets. `boneyard.py` already in `dist_manifest` (W6).\n- **GATE 1.** Full suite GREEN 1163 â€” but the count DIDN'T GROW: the EXECUTE step forgot the per-version regression-test files. **FIX:** added `tests/test_cli_v10.py` (20) + `tests/test_healthcheck_v10.py` (6) mirroring the v9 convention; the healthcheck test DRIVES `check_rnd_v10_surface` and asserts hermeticity (env restored, no `:8777`, stub PTYs + synthetic rows reaped, temp dirs torn down) â€” no walk bug found.\n- **REVIEW (2 independent).** Reviewer A (mechanics): **GO** â€” CLI genuinely read-only (no session start/model call/mutation), healthcheck hermeticity equivalent to v9 with no leak path, the test genuinely proves it, all 4 walk steps non-vacuous, distro clean, strictly additive. Reviewer B (docs + North-Star completeness): **all 3 pillars delivered end-to-end** (verified by reading code) â€” 2 DOC-OVERCLAIMS fixed: Boneyard doc links route through `/artifact` for ALL sources (not `/report` for killed); researchâ†’plan writes only NEXT-PROMPT.md always (HANDOFF.md conditional on a discoverable plan set). CLAUDE.md corrected.\n- **GATE 2 (orch